// Hand-maintained. Edit this list directly when you add or remove a public
// FleetStore method.
//
// The public surface of FleetStore. One list, read by both the main-thread
// client (which method names to proxy) and the await-fleet-store lint rule
// (which calls must be awaited), so the two cannot disagree about what the
// store exposes.
//
// A method missing from this list is not proxied to the worker, so it is
// simply absent on the client — the failure is at the call site, not here.
//
// This header used to say "GENERATED by scratch/gen-manifest.mjs — do not
// hand-edit". No such script has ever existed in the repository; it was a
// one-off in an untracked scratch directory. The claim outlived it and told
// every reader that the only available way to change this file was forbidden.

// Deliberately NOT here — a function crosses each of these boundaries:
//   onEvent: returns an unsubscribe function; the client implements it locally and forwards worker events
//   close: lifecycle, not a query: the client must close the store INSIDE the worker and only then terminate the thread, or the thread dies mid-write
